ishment and  maybe there'll be something more  stringent so nobody knows what the  Commissioner is going to do I've also  suggested that maybe Kraft will impose  on himself a punishment that will be  sufficiently stringent that anyone would  say well yeah that's not that's not too  lenient he is selecting his own  suspension he's selecting his own fine  taking this off the commissioner's plate  because really you know i mean say what  you will about the commissioner he  didn't ask for this one and and he's in  a tough spot now where he's got a  balance those who would say you're being  too lenient versus those who who would  say that you're going too far so if  there is a way that Kraft could fashion  his own punishment that would actually  help the commissioner out of a very  delicate spot so my other question is  how much do the other owners play a part  in a case like this where they have to  figure out you know even if he's  completely you know free of all charges  and walks free and and everything is  thrown out in court you still have the  conduct policy and they can basically  make the argument well it looks bad for  the NFL that he even was named in this  to begin with so my question to you is  the owners so the regular the rest of  the owners are they sitting there  saying well this is the guy who keeps  beating us in Super Bowls and keeps  owning the league or do they say hey  this is one of our guys and this could  happen to you know if you're sitting  there and you're an owner event NFL team  you could be in this position someday  you want your fellow owners to back you  up until Roger Goodell don't don't throw  the book at him take it easy on him it's  a misdemeanor how does that play into  the whole dynamic here well you know  that's a tough balance as well because  what happened with deflate gate there  were multiple reports that there were  owners pushing for a more stringent  punishment of the Patriots because there  was still lingering resentment t